Source: https://github.com/CERALIVE/librga
Comment:
 Generated from the file-level licence census in docs/PROVENANCE.md, which is
 produced by scripts/license-census.sh and fails closed on any tracked file it
 cannot classify. The repository root licence is Apache-2.0, but the tree bundles
 third-party subtrees that are not, so a repository-level claim would be false at
 file granularity. Every non-Rockchip holder and every bundled subtree below has
 its own stanza; packaging/package-contract.sh fails the build if the census
 reports a path this file does not specifically cover.
 .
 Android.mk is the one file whose own header contradicts the root licence: it
 carries a GNU General Public License v3-or-later notice. It is deliberately NOT
 covered by the "Files: *" stanza — the stanza below it overrides that match, per
 the last-match-wins rule of this format. It is an Android NDK build file, the
 Linux build is Meson, and it ships in NO package produced by this repository.
 .
 The four prebuilt libdrm.so binaries under samples/utils/3rdparty/libdrm/lib are
 recorded because a committed shared object is a redistribution obligation that a
 source-header scan would miss. They are sample-only build inputs and are never
 packaged; the shipped library links the system libdrm2 when it links libdrm at
 all.

